@startuml
title 5G Traffic Steering to NGFW/SASE (Runtime Sequence: N4 + N3/N6)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam participantPadding 10
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor UE
participant "gNB\n(5G RAN)" as GNB
participant "AMF\n(Control)" as AMF
participant "SMF\n(Session Control)" as SMF
participant "PCF\n(Policy)" as PCF
participant "UPF\n(User Plane)" as UPF
participant "NGFW/SASE\n(Security Chain)" as NGFW
participant "DN\n(Internet/Enterprise)" as DN

== (A) Precondition ==
note over UE,UPF
UE is already registered (5G-AKA done).
UE now requests / has a PDU Session for internet/enterprise DN.
end note

== (B) PDU Session / Policy Decision ==
UE -> GNB: NAS: PDU Session Establishment Request\n(DNN, S-NSSAI)
GNB -> AMF: N2: Forward NAS message
AMF -> SMF: Create SM Context\n(Nsmf_PDUSession...)

SMF -> PCF: Query policy\n(Npcf_SMPolicyControl)
PCF --> SMF: Policy + Steering intent\n(QoS, which traffic needs inspection)

note right of PCF
Example policy:
- All traffic in enterprise slice -> inspect
- Unknown domains -> inspect
- Trusted apps -> bypass
end note

== (C) SMF programs UPF (N4 PFCP) ==
SMF -> UPF: PFCP Session Establishment/Modify\nInstall rules:
note right of UPF
Rules installed by SMF:
- PDR: match flow (5-tuple/QFI/DNN/slice)
- FAR: action (forward to DN / redirect to NGFW / drop)
- QER: QoS enforcement
- URR: usage report (counters)
end note

UPF --> SMF: PFCP Response (OK)

== (D) User Plane Traffic Begins ==
UE -> GNB: Send packets (YouTube/WhatsApp/etc.)
GNB -> UPF: N3 GTP-U packets\n(User plane)

UPF -> UPF: Classify packet using PDRs

alt Flow requires Security Inspection
  UPF -> NGFW: N6 Steering/Redirect\n(Service chain)
  NGFW -> NGFW: DPI / URLF / IPS checks
  NGFW --> DN: Forward clean traffic
else Trusted / Bypass Flow
  UPF --> DN: N6 Direct traffic
end

== (E) Telemetry / Accounting ==
UPF --> SMF: PFCP Report\n(URR usage: bytes, packets, events)
SMF --> PCF: Optional updates\n(policy/charging triggers)

note bottom
Key learning:
- Steering happens in USER PLANE (UPF).
- Decision/rules come from CONTROL PLANE (SMF/PCF).
- gNB transports user packets (N3) but does not do security inspection.
end note

@enduml
